From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patryk Kowalczyk <papyszoo@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:49:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: the player physics gate names its owner, and can admit
 one run a game frame

The [phys] line reports each interval's gate calls and runs per game frame, the pass a call
belongs to against the right-eye pass that dispatches the job, the PPC core, the lag behind that
pass, the gap between calls and the updater's tail beside its entry. bettervr.json {"playerOnce":1}
turns the gate into a per-frame latch (default off: upstream's right-eye check). Logging and a
switch only; nothing changes with the defaults.
---
